  "sessionContext": [
    "Prefer established packages with multiple maintainers and recent updates.",
    "No high/critical known vulnerabilities; inspect lockfiles and audit data.",
    "Keep dependency changes narrow; explain package and lockfile changes.",
    "uv sync remains unsupported until the host bridge can clear or bind UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT; it can redirect writes outside the workspace.",
    "Before Pixi operations, persist no-build = true in [tool.pixi.workspace.pypi-options] in pyproject.toml (or [workspace.pypi-options] in pixi.toml). Default-feature pypi-options also work, but every environment with no-default-feature = true then needs it on an included feature. Use an explicit --manifest-path to that file; directory discovery is not authorized.",
    "When using uv, encourage persisting [tool.uv] no-build = true in pyproject.toml; keep --no-build on every Maker command because --no-config ignores persisted settings. Never weaken no-build to resolve an unavailable wheel; report the package requiring a source build.",
    "Git pushes require explicit activation with push: true from the canonical repository root. This freezes the origin GitHub URL, current branch, repository hook directory, and hook-tree contents and modes. Use only git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/<activated-branch> from that root. Activation trusts reviewed repository hooks; review them before activation. Global or external hook directories are not included in that trust. Remote, branch, hook-directory, hook-content, and hook-mode changes require review and reactivation."
